                <pb facs="0126" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/>

                <head>Appendix 54</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Extract From Minutes of Meeting of the
                        Shipping Section Held on 26th March, 1919</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Regarding</hi>] <hi rendition="#italic">Transport of Polish Troops to
                        Dantzig</hi></p>
                <p>Mr. Robinson stated that the United States had no enemy ships under their control
                    of suitable draft. He suggested that the ships which the Germans claimed as
                    exceptions which were to be used for maintaining the German forces in the East
                    against Bolchevism, might be available for this purpose.</p>
                <p>It was decided that M. de Lubersac would obtain from the Supreme Economic Council
                    a decision on the point raised by the Germans as to whether the Germans were to
                    be allowed to retain these ships.</p>
            </div>
